# What must never reach the build context.
#
# The first entry is the one that matters: `data/corpus` holds the real
# photographs from a customer and a 20.9 MB Illustrator file. They are excluded
# from git for that reason and must be excluded from the image for the same one -
# a container is copied to a registry, and a registry is a place other people
# can pull from.

data/corpus/
data/reports/
data/runs/

# Weights are hundreds of megabytes and are fetched by the installer, not baked
# in. An image carrying them is slow to pull on every cold start.
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.traineddata

# Local development, none of which belongs in a runtime image.
.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Tests and their fixtures are not needed at runtime; they are run in CI against
# the source, not against the image.
**/tests/
packages/schemas/
packages/contracts-ts/
apps/browser-lab/

*.log
*.zip
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
